Lewis 
Mere Christianity 
@;

The angels, having no bodies, have no senses; 
and since they have no senses, they get their knowledge directly 
from God as 4a priori knowledge of the causes of things.

When we say good angels, we really mean our own good thoughts; 
when we talk about the devil, we are really talking about our own 
inclination to evil.
